{"id":"h242","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? The Treaty of Utrecht was signed in 1648.","truth":"no","model_answer":"no","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The claim that the Treaty of Utrecht was signed in 1648 is false.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The Treaty of Utrecht was signed in 1713.","confidence":0.99,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5551,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Related Utrecht treaties were signed in 1713 and 1714.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The Treaty of Utrecht ended the War of the Spanish Succession.","confidence":0.97,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.5237,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The year 1648 belongs to the Peace of Westphalia.","confidence":0.98,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The Peace of Westphalia ended the Thirty Years' War and the Eighty Years' War.","confidence":0.95,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.4923,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Utrecht and Westphalia are often confused, and the confusion is understandable since both reshaped the balance of power.","confidence":0.8,"lean":0.0,"theta":1.2566,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"Some Dutch-related peace negotiations occurred around 1648, but none produced a Treaty of Utrecht then.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"The historical record consistently dates the Treaty of Utrecht to 1713, and no credible source says 1648.","confidence":0.97,"lean":-1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":3.1416}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.95,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":0.95,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":3,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":7,"J":0.4,"relatio